{
  "myth": "In the dawn of time, there lived two spirits, Aethel the Sower and Kael the Keeper. Aethel possessed five golden seeds, the kernels of existence. He could bury them in his own garden, ensuring only a meager return, or he could offer them to the wild, untamed soil of Kael’s domain. If Aethel trusted Kael, the seeds would be blessed by the sun and rain, multiplying threefold into fifteen shimmering blossoms. The dilemma hung in the air like the scent of ozone. If Kael kept the harvest for himself, he would grow opulent, but the bond of their world would shatter, leaving the earth barren for eternity. If Kael returned a portion of the bounty, they would both flourish, weaving a tapestry of shared prosperity that stretched across the heavens. Aethel held out his palms, the seeds glowing with potential. He chose to release them. Kael stood at the edge of the abyss, the golden light reflecting in his eyes. He realized that the strength of their world rested not on the seeds alone, but on the invisible bridge of trust between them. To give was to risk; to return was to build. Thus, the cycle of reciprocity began, sustaining the stars."
}

